WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.805
A microservice owns a coherent business capability and its data.

00:00:03.955 --> 00:00:09.214
Splitting by technical layer, such as controller service and database service, often

00:00:09.214 --> 00:00:10.529
creates excessive coupling.

00:00:10.679 --> 00:00:16.802
Begin with domain boundaries, team ownership, consistency requirements, and deployment needs.

00:00:16.952 --> 00:00:20.946
A modular monolith can be a better starting point when independent deployment

00:00:20.946 --> 00:00:22.278
is not yet valuable.

00:00:22.428 --> 00:00:28.543
A service boundary introduces network failure, latency, versioning, and operational overhead.

00:00:28.693 --> 00:00:32.453
Keep contracts explicit and avoid cross-service database joins.

00:00:32.603 --> 00:00:35.922
Share identifiers and events rather than entity classes.

00:00:36.072 --> 00:00:40.397
A small shared library may reduce repetition, but a shared domain model

00:00:40.397 --> 00:00:42.559
can force services to upgrade together.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:46.271
Inventory owns products, stock, and reservations.

00:00:46.421 --> 00:00:50.685
Orders owns checkout intent, order status, and outbox events.

00:00:50.835 --> 00:00:55.167
Orders calls the inventory API with its order ID as the reservation

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:55.528
identity.

00:00:55.678 --> 00:01:00.329
It does not query the inventory database or assume a distributed transaction

00:01:00.329 --> 00:01:01.492
spans both databases.

00:01:01.642 --> 00:01:07.582
Design a commerce boundary map including catalog, inventory, orders, payment, and shipping.

00:01:07.732 --> 00:01:12.519
Identify which capabilities could remain modules in one application and which need

00:01:12.519 --> 00:01:14.114
independent scaling or ownership.

00:01:14.264 --> 00:01:19.972
Use concrete reasons for each split: independent release cadence, different availability needs,

00:01:19.972 --> 00:01:22.825
data ownership, or measured scaling pressure.

00:01:22.975 --> 00:01:26.511
Document the added failure modes and communication contracts.

00:01:26.661 --> 00:01:30.206
Do not create a service merely because a domain noun exists.

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:31.027
Question.

00:01:31.177 --> 00:01:34.303
Why is a shared database risky for microservices?

00:01:34.453 --> 00:01:35.029
Answer.

00:01:35.179 --> 00:01:39.806
It allows hidden coupling and independent code changes to violate another service’s

00:01:39.806 --> 00:01:40.192
assumptions.

00:01:40.342 --> 00:01:41.013
Question.

00:01:41.163 --> 00:01:43.348
When would you prefer a modular monolith?

00:01:43.498 --> 00:01:44.075
Answer.

00:01:44.225 --> 00:01:48.627
When domain boundaries are still evolving or the team cannot justify the

00:01:48.627 --> 00:01:50.462
operational cost of independent services.
